.TH TLS-SCANNER 1 "October 2026" "tls-scanner 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tls-scanner \- scan active TLS connections and show the owning process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tls-scanner
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tls-scanner
enumerates established TCP connections on the local machine, filters them to
well-known TLS ports (or all ports), maps each connection to its owning
process, and optionally probes the remote endpoint with a new TLS handshake to
retrieve the negotiated protocol version, cipher suite, and certificate
details.
.PP
The TLS probe creates a
.B new
connection to the remote host and port. It does not intercept or modify the
existing session.
.PP
Running with elevated privileges (root) gives full visibility of connections
owned by other users' processes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-all\-ports
Scan all established TCP connections, not just the common TLS ports
(443, 465, 587, 636, 853, 989, 990, 993, 995, 5223, 8443, 8883).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Timeout in seconds for each TLS probe connection (default: 3).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-probe
Skip TLS handshake probing; only list connections and owning processes.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Number of parallel probe workers (default: 10).
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help message and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tls-scanner
Scan common TLS ports with certificate probing.
.TP
.B tls-scanner \-\-all\-ports
Scan all established TCP connections.
.TP
.B tls-scanner \-\-no\-probe
List connections and processes without probing.
.TP
.B tls-scanner \-\-timeout 5
Use a 5 second probe timeout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including when no connections are found).
.TP
.B 1
A required dependency is missing or too old.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ss (8),
.BR netstat (8),
.BR openssl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Generated packaging for the tls-scanner tool.
